rors is fixed or that the pages open properly.</p>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>What's in it:</strong></p>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li><strong>Sign-in at /admin:</strong><span> email and password only. Nobody can register, only approved admins get in, and there's a sign-out button. Every admin page sends visitors back to the sign-in page unless they're signed in as an admin.</span></li>
<li><strong>Dashboard:</strong><span> cards for total clients, active projects, new enquiries, completed projects and total recorded revenue. It also lists active projects and the latest enquiries.</span></li>
<li><strong>Clients:</strong><span> add, edit and delete clients and see their contact details. Each client shows their projects with the service purchased, the price and a status you can change.</span></li>
<li><strong>Projects:</strong><span> create projects, assign them to clients, and add a description, price and due date. You can drag the progress slider or mark a project complete.</span></li>
<li><strong>Enquiries:</strong><span> see the name, email, phone and message for each one, mark it new, contacted or converted, or delete it. From now on the website's contact form saves every enquiry here as well as emailing you.</span></li>
<li><strong>Look:</strong><span> the same navy and cyan design, a sidebar on desktop and a scrolling menu bar on phones, plus the dark/light switch.</span></li>
</ul>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>Security:</strong><span> all records are stored on Lovable Cloud's free tier, and the database itself blocks anyone who isn't an admin from reading or changing them. No passwords or keys are in the website code.</span></p>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>Your first sign-in:</strong><span> go to /admin and click "Email me a secure set-password link". The link can only go to </span><a href="mailto:rayhanadenga0@gmail.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">rayhanadenga0@gmail.com</a><span>. Open it, choose a password, and you'll land on the dashboard. Use the same button if you ever forget your password.</span></p>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>Not finished yet:</strong></p>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li><strong>The old Client Hub at /dashboard:</strong><span> it's unchanged and still keeps its data only in your browser.</span></li>
<li><strong>Testing:</strong><span> I haven't added a check for the dashboard figures or tried the full sign-in in the preview.</span></li>
</ul>
<p dir="ltr">Reply "continue" and I'll check for errors, test the sign-in, and point the old /dashboard page to the new admin area.</p></div><div class="flex items-center" data-testid="agent-message-toolbar" data-message-copy-text="Your private admin area is built, but I ran out of time before I could check it. I haven't confirmed that the last round of errors is fixed or that the pages open properly.

What's in it:
- Sign-in at /admin: email and password only. Nobody can register, only approved admins get in, and there's a sign-out button. Every admin page sends visitors back to the sign-in page unless they're signed in as an admin.
- Dashboard: cards for total clients, active projects, new enquiries, completed projects and total recorded revenue. It also lists active projects and the latest enquiries.
- Clients: add, edit and delete clients and see their contact details. Each client shows their projects with the service purchased, the price and a status you can change.
- Projects: create projects, assign them to clients, and add a description, price and due date. You can drag the progress slider or mark a project complete.
- Enquiries: see the name, email, phone and message for each one, mark it new, contacted or converted, or delete it. From now on the website's contact form saves every enquiry here as well as emailing you.
- Look: the same navy and cyan design, a sidebar on desktop and a scrolling menu bar on phones, plus the dark/light switch.

Security: all records are stored on Lovable Cloud's free tier, and the database itself blocks anyone who isn't an admin from reading or changing them. No passwords or keys are in the website code.

Your first sign-in: go to /admin and click &quot;Email me a secure set-password link&quot;. The link can only go to rayhanadenga0@gmail.com. Open it, choose a password, and you'll land on the dashboard. Use the same button if you ever forget your password.

Not finished yet:
- The old Client Hub at /dashboard: it's unchanged and still keeps its data only in your browser.
- Testing: I haven't added a check for the dashboard figures or tried the full sign-in in the preview.

Reply &quot;continue&quot; and I'll check for errors, test the sign-in, and point the old /dashboard page to the new admin area.

